# ClaimTrack walkthrough: one claim's whole life.
# Run the requests in order ("Send Request" above each one) in VS Code with the REST Client
# extension, or in Visual Studio.
#
# Needs: `docker compose up` running, and .env in this folder (the demo password is read from it,
# so it never has to be typed into this file).
# For `dotnet run` instead of Docker, change @api to http://localhost:5016.

@api = http://localhost:8080
@password = {{$dotenv DEMO_PASSWORD}}

### Log in as each role
# @name priya
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "priya.singh@claimtrack.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
# @name supervisor
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "supervisor@claimtrack.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
# @name adjuster
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "adjuster1@claimtrack.test", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 1. The policyholder lists her policies (the first one is her active Auto policy)
# @name policies
GET {{api}}/api/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 1b. ...and submits a claim against it
# @name claim
POST {{api}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyId": "{{policies.response.body.$[0].id}}",
  "incidentDate": "{{$datetime 'YYYY-MM-DD'}}",
  "description": "Rear-ended at a red light; rear bumper and trunk damaged.",
  "claimedAmount": 2400.00
}

### 2. The supervisor lists the adjusters (sorted by name, so Jane Doe = adjuster1 comes first)
# @name adjusters
GET {{api}}/api/users?role=Adjuster
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2b. ...and assigns the claim to the first one
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{claim.response.body.$.id}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "adjusterId": "{{adjusters.response.body.$[0].id}}" }

### 3. The adjuster starts the review
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{claim.response.body.$.id}}/start-review
Authorization: Bearer {{adjuster.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 3b. ...and recommends
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{claim.response.body.$.id}}/recommendation
Authorization: Bearer {{adjuster.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "recommendation": "Approve", "notes": "Repair estimate matches the photos and the police report." }

### 4. The supervisor decides (to deny instead: "decision": "Deny", "reason": "<at least 10 characters>")
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{claim.response.body.$.id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "Approve" }

### 5. The policyholder reads the full history
GET {{api}}/api/claims/{{claim.response.body.$.id}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Lists: filtered, sorted, paged
GET {{api}}/api/claims?status=Approved&sort=-claimedAmount&pageSize=2
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Errors: withdrawing an approved claim → 409
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{claim.response.body.$.id}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Errors: page size over 100 → 400
GET {{api}}/api/claims?pageSize=500
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Errors: a supervisor can't submit claims → 403
POST {{api}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}
